 "text": "Hi, how are you feeling? Start with something personal and light, like their favorite TV show or the last place they traveled. Then work your way into the main topic, asking them to expand. That works nicely. Then you can go deeper if they mention it, like how they learned the recipe, or if they failed mysteriously. That's really common. You could ask for few seconds to think before you answer, or you could just pause the recording and start again. It' a good idea. Sending them a day before gives them time to think and read, and you can keep any surprises for the live recording. Anytime. Enjoy the interview.",
